Title: Weather Log
Credit: written by
Author: the Method Reader project
Draft date: an invented sample

INT. RECORDING HUT - NIGHT

A plywood room on stilts. A barometer, a kettle, a logbook open to a page of pencil columns.

ODA (40s) taps the barometer glass twice and writes a number down.

ODA
Nine ninety-one. Falling.

PELL (60s) comes in from the dark, shaking rain off a hood.

PELL
(not looking up)
It was falling at six as well.

ODA
It was falling *slowly* at six.

[[A note for the reader: invisible in the book.]]

EXT. MAST - CONTINUOUS

The anemometer cups spin so fast they blur.

PELL
Twenty knots.

ODA ^
Twenty-five.

CUT TO:

INT. RECORDING HUT - LATER

The kettle boils dry. Neither of them moves to it.

ODA
We log it, we send it, and we wait.

PELL
**We wait.**

> THE END <
